<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/coastal-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/coastal-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/coastal-home.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Pascagoula</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Gulf Coast</p><h1>Pascagoula and Coastal Jackson County Claim Appraisal</h1><p class="lede">Pascagoula sits on the eastern end of the Mississippi Coast, where surge, wind and split policies all meet. If your carrier’s estimate won’t pay for a proper repair, appraisal can settle the amount.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Jackson County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>Gulf Coast</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Pascagoula</li><li>Beach Boulevard</li><li>Moss Point</li><li>Gautier</li><li>Escatawpa</li><li>Vancleave</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Coastal Jackson County has raised homes rebuilt after Katrina, older brick and frame homes from the shipyard boom years, manufactured homes in rural areas, and newer subdivisions inland.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Aug 29, 2005</b><span>Hurricane Katrina’s storm surge and wind</span></li><li><b>Aug 2012</b><span>Hurricane Isaac’s rain and surge</span></li><li><b>Oct 28, 2020</b><span>Hurricane Zeta’s strong wind across the Coast</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Hurricane surge and wind</li><li>MWUA wind policy disputes</li><li>Named-storm percentage deductibles</li><li>River and bayou flooding</li><li>Wind-driven rain and roof damage</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Jackson County, not the city of Jackson</h2>
<p>A quick clarification first: Jackson County is the easternmost coastal county in Mississippi. It is not the city of Jackson, which sits in Hinds County in the middle of the state. Pascagoula is the county seat of Jackson County, at the mouth of the Pascagoula River near the eastern state line.</p>
<p>Pascagoula is a shipbuilding town. The shipyard has been the area’s largest employer for generations, and much of the housing in Pascagoula, Moss Point and Gautier was built to house its workforce. Ocean Springs sits at the western end of the county.</p>

<h2>Hurricanes on the eastern Coast</h2>
<p>Hurricane Katrina’s surge on August 29, 2005 flooded large parts of Pascagoula and pushed up the river and bayous into Moss Point and Gautier. Wind damage followed far beyond the surge line. The claim fights that followed, over wind versus water and anti-concurrent-causation clauses, lasted for years.</p>
<p>Since then, Hurricane Isaac in August 2012 brought heavy rain and surge, and Hurricane Zeta, which made landfall in Louisiana on October 28, 2020, sent strong wind across the Coast, including Jackson County.</p>

<h2>Split policies in the MWUA territory</h2>
<p>Jackson County is one of the six southernmost counties served by the Mississippi Windstorm Underwriting Association. Many Pascagoula owners have:</p>
<ul>
<li>a homeowners policy that excludes wind,</li>
<li>an MWUA policy for wind and hail, and</li>
<li>a separate flood policy, usually through the NFIP.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each policy has its own deductible and, often, its own appraisal clause. Wind deductibles on the Coast are frequently a percentage of Coverage A. Our <a href="/claim-calculator-suite/wind-water-split-estimator/">wind and water split estimator</a> can help you think through how a loss might be divided.</p>
<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">What appraisal can and can’t do here</b><p>Appraisal won’t decide whether wind or water caused a loss; that is generally a coverage question. It can set the amount of the wind damage, or of each part of a loss, once coverage is accepted.</p></div>

<h2>Homes in Pascagoula, Moss Point and Gautier</h2>
<p>Older neighborhoods near Downtown Pascagoula and along Beach Boulevard have brick and frame homes from the shipyard boom years, many of them repaired or raised after 2005. Moss Point and Escatawpa mix older homes with rural property along the rivers. Gautier and Vancleave include newer subdivisions and manufactured homes.</p>
<h3>Disputes we see often</h3>
<ul>
<li>Raised homes priced without the access equipment and labor they need.</li>
<li>Roof estimates that ignore code requirements for wind resistance on a full replacement.</li>
<li>Manufactured homes with roof and skirting damage written as minor repairs.</li>
<li>Interior water damage assigned to flood when the roof was opened by wind.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Next steps</h2>
<p>If you and your carrier agree the loss is covered but not on what it costs, we can review the estimate and, where your policy allows, represent you through appraisal. See our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/hurricane-named-storm-appraisal/">hurricane and named-storm appraisal</a> service. We serve Pascagoula, Moss Point, Gautier, Ocean Springs and the rest of Jackson County. Confirm your deadlines with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Pascagoula</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Pascagoula and the rest of Jackson County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/hurricane-named-storm-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Named Storm Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Pascagoula claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Is Jackson County the same as the city of Jackson?</summary><p>No. Jackson County is on the Gulf Coast, with Pascagoula as its county seat. The city of Jackson is the state capital, mostly in Hinds County.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need separate appraisals for my wind policy and my homeowners policy?</summary><p>Often, yes. Each policy has its own appraisal clause and carrier. If both policies are disputed, they may proceed separately, though the same facts and photos usually support both.</p></details></div>
